  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Milwaukee's bullpen turns any deficit into a chasm once the inning breaks in its favor.",
    "what_this_means": "Bryce Eldridge hit one in the eighth. Two more runs that mattered only to the scoreboard. The Giants never led this game. They trailed after the third inning and never recovered, which is the real story here. Landen Roupp lasted 3.2 innings and gave up four runs, and then the bullpen. Brubaker, Foley, Winn. Held the wreckage steady for 5.1 innings after. But the offense couldn't sustain anything. Nine strikeouts. Two runners left on in the first, two more in the ninth. This is inconsistency showing teeth. When you fall behind early and have nowhere to go but down, having one hitter who can reach the stands changes nothing.",
    "what_to_watch": "Shane Drohan starts tonight for Milwaukee with a 3.51 ERA, and Logan Webb gets the ball for the Giants at 12:45 PT. A spot where both teams are looking to reset from a game that was decided by the fifth inning.",
